# Shared checkout isolation

- Never use the shared local `main` checkout as the working directory for implementation work.
- Do not edit, stage, commit, rebase, merge, reset, install dependencies, run tests/builds, or start/stop dev servers from that checkout.
- Create or use an isolated worktree and feature branch for all changes and verification.
- Integrate through a reviewable GitHub pull request; merge the PR remotely, then leave the shared checkout untouched unless the user explicitly asks to sync it.
- Preserve unrelated changes in every checkout. Never clean or reset the shared checkout to make a task easier.
